{"name":"Peacock Purple","hex":"#513843","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peacock","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male peafowl, especially Pavo cristatus, notable for its brilliant iridescently ocellated tail.","A peafowl (of the genus Pavo or Afropavo), either male or female."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strut about proudly or haughtily.","To engage in peacocking, ostentatious dress or behaviour to impress women."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peacock"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peafowl","blocks":[{"text":"Peafowl is a common name for two bird species of the genus Pavo and one species of the closely related genus Afropavo within the tribe Pavonini of the family Phasianidae. Male peafowl are referred to as peacocks, and female peafowl are referred to as peahens. Despite this, peacock is usually used to refer to both sexes, in common language."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Peacock_Plumage.jpg/330px-Peacock_Plumage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peafowl","wikidata":"Q201251"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Eggs_of_Peafowl_at_Aravath_Kasaragod.jpg/500px-Eggs_of_Peafowl_at_Aravath_Kasaragod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Eggs_of_Peafowl_at_Aravath_Kasaragod.jpg/500px-Eggs_of_Peafowl_at_Aravath_Kasaragod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEggs_of_Peafowl_at_Aravath_Kasaragod.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Baby_Peacock_%2818131813108%29.jpg/500px-Baby_Peacock_%2818131813108%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Baby_Peacock_%2818131813108%29.jpg/1280px-Baby_Peacock_%2818131813108%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Baby_Peacock_%2818131813108%29.jpg/500px-Baby_Peacock_%2818131813108%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaby_Peacock_(18131813108).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Peacock-JS.jpg/500px-Peacock-JS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser